# Third-party notices

The `Krilla` package contains a native library statically linked from the Rust crates listed
below. Their licences require that this notice accompany any binary distribution, so it ships
inside the package alongside Krilla's own [MIT licence](../../license.txt).

Krilla takes each dual-licensed crate under the **MIT** arm where one is offered.

This file is generated. Do not edit it by hand — run:

```
cargo about generate --config about.toml about.hbs -o ../src/Krilla/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
```

## The Rust standard library

Every build statically links the Rust standard library, which is distributed under `MIT OR
Apache-2.0` and whose own `COPYRIGHT` file carries further notices for LLVM and compiler-rt
(`Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception`). It is not a crate in the dependency graph, so it does not
appear in the list below; its notices are available at
<https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/master/COPYRIGHT>.

